<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-how-to-make-easy-homemade-tzatziki-a-step-by-step-guide">How to Make Easy Homemade Tzatziki: A Step-by-Step Guide</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Making a delicious tzatziki with yogurt, shredded cucumber, and lemon juice doesn&rsquo;t require any special cooking techniques, so anyone can do it.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="744" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/Greek-tzatziki-sauce.jpg" alt="A collage of images showing how to strain grated cucumber and make the yogurt mixture." class="wp-image-81913" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/Greek-tzatziki-sauce.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/Greek-tzatziki-sauce-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/Greek-tzatziki-sauce-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/Greek-tzatziki-sauce-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/Greek-tzatziki-sauce-150x93.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/Greek-tzatziki-sauce.jpg"></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Step 1 &ndash; Grate and drain the cucumber:</strong> Using the large holes of a box grater, grate the peeled cucumber and transfer it to a fine-mesh strainer. Press down with a spatula to release the excess moisture. I usually let it sit for a few minutes to help the juices drain completely.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Once drained, you should have about 1 cup of grated cucumber.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Alternatively, you can wrap the shredded cucumber in a clean tea towel and squeeze it by hand to remove as much liquid as possible.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Step 2 &ndash; Whisk the yogurt base:</strong> In a medium bowl, combine the Greek yogurt, freshly squeezed lemon juice, minced garlic, salt, and black pepper.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Whisk until smooth and creamy. This is also a good time to give it a quick taste and adjust the seasoning if needed.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="744" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/Greek-yogurt-cucumber-sauce.jpg" alt="A collage of photos showing how to make tzatziki from scratch." class="wp-image-81914" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/Greek-yogurt-cucumber-sauce.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/Greek-yogurt-cucumber-sauce-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/Greek-yogurt-cucumber-sauce-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/Greek-yogurt-cucumber-sauce-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/Greek-yogurt-cucumber-sauce-150x93.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/Greek-yogurt-cucumber-sauce.jpg"></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Step 3 &ndash; Add cucumber and herbs:</strong> Fold in the drained cucumber and fresh dill or mint. Mix until everything is evenly combined.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Step 4 &ndash; Cover and chill:</strong><strong><br></strong>You can serve it right away, but if you have the time, cover and let it rest in the fridge for at least 30 minutes. This allows the flavors to meld and deepen.</p>


