r yogurt, lemon juice, minced garlic, salt and pepper.</span></div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-15932-step-0-2" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Using a spatula, fold in the cucumber and dill.  Transfer to a bowl.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/tzatziki-dip-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Person making the tzatziki in a bowl." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/tzatziki-dip-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/tzatziki-dip-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/tzatziki-dip-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/tzatziki-dip-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/tzatziki-dip.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/tzatziki-dip.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-15932-step-0-3" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">If you have time, cover with plastic, and let it sit in the fridge for a few hours before serving.</span></div></li></ul></div></div>
